## Context

- cd-gpx4-ferroptosis-convergence: All 6 analyst tasks (Phase 2+3) completed. Partial validation: 1.5/4 success criteria met.
- SC1 FAILED: GPX4 bulk expression has zero predictive value for anti-TNF response (AUC=0.530, all cohorts p>0.6).
- SC2 MET: Ferroptosis elevated in inflammatory macrophages and monocytes in IL-23-high (FDR=2.2e-9).
- SC3 MET: GPX4 correlates with fibrosis markers in 2/3 bulk cohorts (GSE12251 rho=0.549, GSE73661 rho=0.723). Pooled correlations inflated by batch effects.
- SC4 MARGINAL: FFI AUC=0.658 but delta over baseline is +0.001 (useless).
- Cross-compartment scRNA-seq correlations: all non-significant (n=23 underpowered). Ferroptosis module showed near-significant trends (rho~0.35, p~0.10).
- ILC2 untestable (not annotated in GSE134809). Task 6 showed directionally consistent Th17 depletion in low-GPX4 samples (d=-0.52) but non-significant.
- Created task #1675 for research_director to evaluate findings.
- Scripts: 04_cross_compartment_correlation.py, 05_gpx4_loso_cv.py, 06_scrna_bulk_crossref.py, 07_phase3_fibrosis_iron.py in src/crohns/cd_gpx4_ferroptosis_convergence/
- Next: GSE282122 (~1M cells) could rescue cross-compartment correlations with more power and potentially ILC2 annotation.
